# Zone identity (M4 polish): open countryside - low bushes make the border (a few round trees stay inside), wildflowers dot the grass.
# Ruta 1 - Villa Aliso <-> Ciudad Nodo (Route 1; M4-D: the north gate is the real way to Ciudad Nodo). column = i, row = j; the village is at the +j end (south, the bottom
# of the grid: screen down-left), Ciudad Nodo at j=0 (north, screen up-right). Winding path, tall-grass patches with the wild
# encounter table, three rows of one-way ledges facing south (hop SW = +j, i.e. Down + Left), a roaming wild creature.
@map ruta_1
@size 20 36
@interior no
@area ruta_1
@bg 0
@fill grass
@spawn south 9 34 N
@spawn north 9 1 S            # arriving from Ciudad Nodo (one tile inside the north exit)
@flag clerk_gave 31           # the clerk's Salve was given (once)
@var result 4                 # battle result (0 lost, 1 won, 2 ran, 3 caught); same variable as the lab's
@encounters grass rate=25     # encounter when rand8 < 25 (9.8 %) on every step into tall grass
# species lv_min lv_max weight (Route 1: only the songbird and the rodent)
  flitter 2 5 55
  muncrit 2 5 45
@end
# Open ground (contract 63, transit road): a step onto plain ground (not tall grass, water, a door, a ledge, an arrow floor) rolls this table when rand8 < 2 (2/256 per step).
@open_rate 2
# Roaming wild creatures (contract 55, PILOT): up to 2 creatures wander the open ground (plain grass, path, flowers: never the tall grass, the ledges, the doors) and the
# grass table's species / levels are drawn when each (re)appears; touching one starts that wild battle, after it a new one comes 30 steps later, out of view.
@roam 2 table=grass area=.=f period=1800
@legend
  .  tile=grass
  =  tile=path
  g  tile=tall_grass
  f  tile=flowers
  T  object=tree              # the few trees that stay (the borders are bushes now)
  B  object=bush              # low bushes: the field's border (open countryside)
  r  object=rock
  v  ledge=SW                 # one-way ledge: hop over it toward +j (Down + Left)
  S  object=sign interact=look text=route1.sign
  L  object=sign interact=look text=route1.ledge
  N  tile=path                # the way to Ciudad Nodo (warp below)
  s  tile=path                # the way home (warp below)
  # Mart clerk: gives a Salve on Route 1 (once); he stands beside the path at the south end, looking at it
  k  npc=vecino id=clerk face=NW script=clerk
  H  tile=grass hidden=salve   # hidden (contract 80, hidden items)
@grid
  BBBBBBBBBNNBBBBBBBBB
  B........==........B
  B....T...==...TT...B
  B.ggggg..==......f.B
  B.ggggg..==.r...f..B
  B.ggggg..==........B
  Bvvvvvv..==..vvvvvvB
  Bf.......==........B
  B..ff....==....TT..B
  B...TT...===...T...B
  B.f.......==..f....B
  Bvvvvvvvv.==..vvvvvB
  B......f..===...f..B
  B..gggggg..==...f..B
  B..gggggg..==.gggg.B
  B..gggggg..==.gggg.B
  B..gggggg.===fgggg.B
  BH.gggggg.==..gggg.B
  B.........==..gggg.B
  B.TT......==..gggg.B
  B.T......===....TT.B
  B.f......==........B
  Bvvvvvvv.==.vvvvvvvB
  B........==.f..f...B
  B.....T.L==...TT.f.B
  B........==...T....B
  BT.......==.gggggg.B
  B..gggg..==.gggggg.B
  B..gggg..==.gggggg.B
  B.fgggg..==.gggggg.B
  B.....f..==.gggggg.B
  B..T.r...==...r....B
  B.......S==k...fT..B
  B....f.T.==..TT....B
  B.T......==......T.B
  BBBBBBBBBssBBBBBBBBB
@warp s -> villa_aliso spawn=route1
@warp N -> ciudad_nodo spawn=south
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mart clerk: "I work at the Mart in Ciudad Nodo. Take this free sample" = a Salve, once. give_item leaves how
# many were really added in var 0 (0 = bag full: he keeps it for later and the flag stays clear).
@script clerk npc
    jf clerk_gave after
    say route1.clerk.a
    give_item salve 1
    jv 0 0 full
    say route1.clerk.got
    setf clerk_gave
    end
  full:
    say route1.clerk.full
    end
  after:
    say route1.clerk.b
@end
